<title>UK: Brokers place 30 mln shares in Sainsbury.</title>
<headline>Brokers place 30 mln shares in Sainsbury.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 30 million shares in supermarket chain Sainsbury Plc were being placed in the market at 347p by SBC Warburg, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In mid-morning, shares in Sainsbury were trading 6-1/2p down on last night at 357-1/2p.  </p>
<p>The stock was placed by institutions and was not Sainsbury family stock, market sources said.</p>
<p>Sainsbury shares slipped earlier on Thursday after NatWest Securities downgraded its recommendation on the stock to &quot;reduce&quot; from &quot;trading sell&quot; and cut its profit forecasts.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
